sentences.t:
El buen Campeador la su cara tornava,
vío que entrellos y el castiello mucho avié grant plaça;
mandó tornar la seña, a priessa espoloneavan.

sentences.l:
The good Campeador the his face turned,
he-saw that between-them and the castle much there-was great space;
he-ordered to-turn the banner, in haste they-spurred.

sentences.t:
Mio Çid e Álbar Fáñez adelant aguijavan;
tienen buenos cavallos, sabet, a su guisa les andan;
entrellos y el castiello en essora entravan.

sentences.l:
My Çid and Álbar Fáñez ahead spurred;
they-have good horses, know-ye, at their will to-them they-go;
between-them and the castle at-that-hour they-entered.

sentences.t:
Oíd a mí Álbar Fáñez e todos los cavalleros!
En este castiello grand aver avemos preso;
los moros yacen muertos, de bivos pocos veo.

sentences.l:
Hear me, Álbar Fáñez and all the knights!
In this castle great wealth we-have taken;
the Moors lie dead, of living few I-see.
